# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore — gchis66/portfolio-site
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. Anything committed here is world-readable forever, even
# after deletion, because it stays in git history.
#
# Intent: `git add -A` should be safe to run without thinking. Everything the
# site and the voice agent need to run is tracked. Everything else, especially
# operational notes containing infrastructure identifiers, is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# === OPERATIONAL RUNBOOKS =================================================
# Click-by-click AWS console instructions. These contain the account ID,
# CloudFront distribution ID, API Gateway IDs, IAM role names, and SSM
# parameter paths. None of it is a credential, but together it is a map of the
# infrastructure and there is no reason to publish it.
RUNBOOK-*.md


# === AMBASSADOR: PLANNING AND KNOWLEDGE BASE ==============================
# The spec is a design document with resource identifiers, cost figures, and
# threat-model notes. The public version of this is prod/talk/architecture.
ambassador/SPEC.md

# The knowledge base is the agent's source material: skills with honesty tags,
# comp band, notice period, employment status, boundary rules, and refusal
# wording. Publishing it hands anyone the exact instructions the agent follows,
# including what it is told to decline and how. It also contains the internal
# rationale for what to say about the layoff.
ambassador/kb/

# Build scripts for the index and prompt. Not needed by anything in prod, and
# they encode the chunking and alias tuning.
ambassador/scripts/

# Component README stubs and the infra resource inventory (invoke URLs,
# resource names, provisioning state).
ambassador/infra/
ambassador/**/README.md


# === RESUME SOURCE ========================================================
# resume/ is the HTML source and a duplicate PDF. The deployed copy lives at
# prod/Gregory_Chisholm_Resume.pdf, which IS tracked. Keeping the source out
# avoids a second copy drifting out of sync.
resume/


# === DRAFTS AND NOTES =====================================================
# Blog drafts are published on Medium; the markdown source is not needed here.
blog/

# Planning docs, wherever they land.
positioning-updates.md
*-notes.md
*-draft.md
TODO.md
NOTES.md


# === SECRETS: NEVER COMMIT ================================================
# Nothing below should ever exist in this repo. Listed defensively so an
# accidental `git add -A` cannot pick one up.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*credentials*
*secret*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
aws-exports.js


# === BUILD ARTIFACTS AND DEPENDENCIES =====================================
node_modules/
package-lock.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.zip


# === EDITOR AND OS ========================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.hermes/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT STAYS TRACKED, AND WHY
#
#   prod/                      The deployed site. S3 syncs from here with
#                              --delete, so anything missing gets removed from
#                              the live bucket.
#   lambda/index.mjs           VisitorCountFunc source.
#   ambassador/lambda/**/*.mjs Session broker and kb-search source. Worth
#                              publishing: it is the interesting engineering,
#                              it holds no credentials (the key is read from
#                              SSM at runtime), and it is referenced from the
#                              public architecture page.
#   .github/workflows/         Deploy pipeline. Uses OIDC, no static keys.
#
# ONE THING TO FIX SEPARATELY: RUNBOOK-oidc.md and ambassador/SPEC.md are
# already in git history from earlier commits. Adding them here stops FUTURE
# commits but does not remove what is already published. See the note in
# positioning-updates.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
